    "badgeColor": "border-amber-500/60 bg-amber-950/80 text-amber-300",
    "title": {
      "en": "Minimum Deposit on AH Being Reduced to 1 Copper Soon in WoW: Forever",
      "es": "El depósito mínimo en AH se reducirá a 1 cobre pronto en WoW: Forever"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Minimum Deposit on AH Being Reduced to 1 Copper Soon in WoW: Forever...",
      "es": "El depósito mínimo en AH se reducirá a 1 cobre pronto en WoW: para siempre..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6aee679d497249.41995111\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">Kris Zierhut has announced that the minimum deposit on the Auction House on WoW: Forever will be changed soon.<br><br>When WoW: Forever launched, the minimum deposit for the Auction House <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/minimum-deposit-of-1-silver-required-to-list-items-at-auction-house-in-wow-383774\" data-contiguous=\"true\">had been increased to 1 Silver</a>. This adds a lot of risk to players in the early economy, as losing 1 Silver every time you don't sell an item can quickly add up, especially when money is tight. In an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QtGf1aJUowU\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">interview with Crix</a>, Kris Zierhut discusses how they handle internal disagreements. At the end of the segment, he addresses the minimum deposit change, noting that it will be changing soon.<div class=\"quote-box exclude-units\" data-type=\"user\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\">Kris Zierhut<span class=\"quote-said-text\"> said: </span></div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">[...]Maybe the minimum price on the Auction House should be 1 Copper, and not 1 Silver for deposits. We were just talking about that one earlier today and after talking about it with people more, yes, we're changing it back to one copper as the minimum deposit. That's coming. Not yet, but coming.</div></div>Whenever this change is live, players will no longer need to take on a significant risk when putting items on the Auction House.<h2 id=\"deposit-formula\" class=\"heading-size-2 heading-bar\"><span data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Deposit Formula</span></h2>When players list an item on the Auction House, a deposit is required which is given back to players if the item successfully sells, but is lost if the item is cancelled or the Auction expires. After this change goes live, the deposit requirement should return to the WoW: Classic formula and depends on the item's Vendor Price and the duration:<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"markup-table-wrapper\"><table class=\"exclude-units grid\" style=\"width: 800px; max-width: 100%;\"><tbody data-markup-content-target=\"1\"><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>Duration</b></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>Deposit Cost</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">2 Hours</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">5% of Vendor Price</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">8 Hours</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">20% of Vendor Price</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">24 Hours</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">60% of Vendor Price</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>\n            \n            <noscript>Kris Zierhut has announced that the minimum deposit on the Auction House on WoW: Forever will be changed soon.<br /><br />When WoW: Forever launched, the minimum deposit for the Auction House <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/minimum-deposit-of-1-silver-required-to-list-items-at-auction-house-in-wow-383774\">had been increased to 1 Silver</a>. This adds a lot of risk to players in the early economy, as losing 1 Silver every time you don't sell an item can quickly add up, especially when money is tight. In an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QtGf1aJUowU\" rel=\"nofollow\">interview with Crix</a>, Kris Zierhut discusses how they handle internal disagreements. At the end of the segment, he addresses the minimum deposit change, noting that it will be changing soon.<br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\"><h2 class=\"heading-size-2\">Kris Zierhut</h2>Maybe the minimum price on the Auction House should be 1 Copper, and not 1 Silver for deposits. We were just talking about that one earlier today and after talking about it with people more, yes, we're changing it back to one copper as the minimum deposit. That's coming. Not yet, but coming.</div><br /><br />Whenever this change is live, players will no longer need to take on a significant risk when putting items on the Auction House.<br /><br /><h2 class=\"heading-size-2\">Deposit Formula</h2><br /><br />When players list an item on the Auction House, a deposit is required which is given back to players if the item successfully sells, but is lost if the item is cancelled or the Auction expires. After this change goes live, the deposit requirement should return to the WoW: Classic formula and depends on the item's Vendor Price and the duration:<br /><br /><table><tr><td><b>Duration</b></td><td><b>Deposit Cost</b></td></tr><br /><tr><td>2 Hours</td><td>5% of Vendor Price</td></tr><br /><tr><td>8 Hours</td><td>20% of Vendor Price</td></tr><br /><tr><td>24 Hours</td><td>60% of Vendor Price</td></tr></table></noscript>            \n        ",
